# recomp_lift manifest for AngryBirdsStarWars.exe (PC, v1.5.0).
# Line based:
#
#   entry <hexva> [name]   extra function entry point
#   name  <hexva> <name>   name a function (comments in generated code)
#   probe <hexva> [name]   call recomp::Probe() on entry (runtime logs it)
#   resume <hexva>         this call/jmp abandons the current call chain
#                          (SEH, longjmp): throw GuestResume to the owning
#                          frame
#   setjmp <hexva> [name]  a setjmp function: its callers catch
#                          GuestResume, its return points become entries
#   replace <hexva> [name] src/ defines f_<VA>; the lifted body becomes
#                          f_<VA>_lifted
#   native <hexva> <name>  replaced by a shared native function
#                          (recomp::native::<name>)
#   host <hexva> <symbol>  an extern "C" void SYMBOL(Ctx&, uint64_t)

# setjmp/longjmp (MSVC 2010 CRT, msvcr100.dll): located below.

# Native libmpg123 replacement (eliminates startup MP3 decode freeze)
replace 005067C0 mpg123_init
replace 00507070 mpg123_new
replace 00507010 mpg123_delete
replace 00507090 mpg123_open_feed
replace 00506C00 mpg123_feed
replace 00506C50 mpg123_decode
replace 00506D70 mpg123_getformat
replace 00506DD0 mpg123_tell
replace 00506E80 mpg123_feedseek
